# Line endings are LF, everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# This project is edited from Windows and its git is sometimes run from WSL, on
# the same working tree. Windows git had core.autocrlf=true, so it checked
# files out as CRLF and converted back when diffing; WSL git has its own
# config, saw CRLF against an LF index, and reported every line of every file
# as changed. Both were behaving correctly and the working tree could not
# satisfy both.
#
# `eol=lf` takes the decision away from whichever git happens to run. Nothing
# here needs CRLF: Python, the Arduino toolchain and every editor involved
# handle LF on Windows without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.jpg  binary
*.png  binary
*.bin  binary
*.hex  binary
